{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"urwithajit9.evnx","latestVersion":"0.12.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Manage .env files — validate, scan for secrets, convert formats, and sync them end-to-end encrypted","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/urwithajit9/evnx/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Manage .env files — validate, scan for secrets, convert formats, and sync them end-to-end encrypted","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/urwithajit9/evnx/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"evnx is a local-first CLI for .env files: validate syntax, scan for committed credentials and for keys a build would publish to the browser, and convert to 14 deployment formats.\n\nIt also syncs them through evnx cloud, end-to-end encrypted: values are encrypted on your machine under a key derived from your master password, so the server stores only ciphertext and cannot read them. Vaults can be shared, and revoking a member rotates the key and re-encrypts every version.","name":"evnx","packageUrl":"https://www.evnx.dev","publisher":"Ajit Kumar","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/urwithajit9/evnx/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/urwithajit9","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/urwithajit9/evnx/releases/tag/v0.12.0","tags":["cli","dotenv","encryption","env","environment-variables","secrets","security","vault"]}},"longDescription":"evnx is a local-first CLI for .env files: validate syntax, scan for committed credentials and for keys a build would publish to the browser, and convert to 14 deployment formats.\n\nIt also syncs them through evnx cloud, end-to-end encrypted: values are encrypted on your machine under a key derived from your master password, so the server stores only ciphertext and cannot read them. Vaults can be shared, and revoking a member rotates the key and re-encrypts every version.","name":"evnx","packageUrl":"https://www.evnx.dev","publi